// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Print Processor Persistence Via Registry
// Sigma ID: 54f43364-0af7-4bc4-abf7-5d1d63fb88a1
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: ialivrd
// Date: 2026-10-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1547.012
// Description: Detects the registration of a new print processor through the "Print Processors" registry key.
//   Print processors are DLLs that are loaded by the print spooler service (spoolsv.exe), which runs
//   as SYSTEM. Adversaries may abuse this mechanism to execute malicious DLLs for persistence and/or
//   privilege escalation.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate installation of third-party printer software that registers its own print processor
// References:
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/2020/05/21/no-game-over-winnti-group/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/printdocs/addprintprocessor
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/4ff1a4fb9b90c019e441903afb0f48d3ec1a084e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_win_print_processor_persistence.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 2 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Control\\Print\\Environments.*$" and RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Print Processors.*$") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\spoolsv.exe" and RegistryValueData endswith "winprint.dll")))
